I have solid coverage of the build system and driver source. Let me summarize the recorded traces.

## Summary

**Subject**: AMG2023 (LLNL) — builds a single executable `amg` from `amg.c`, a driver that constructs 3D 7-point or 27-point Laplacian linear systems (distributed across an MPI `P x Q x R` logical grid) and solves them with hypre's BoomerAMG-preconditioned PCG or GMRES.

I recorded **four variants**, distinguished by real build-system evidence (`CMakeLists.txt` options `AMG_WITH_MPI/OMP/CUDA/HIP`, `Makefile` CUDA/HIP paths):

1. **amg2023 / cpu-mpi** — baseline MPI-only build. SPMD, process/mpi parallelism, mixed collective+neighbor-style communication inferred from the PxQxR domain decomposition and repeated `hypre_MPI_Barrier` synchronization at each AMG setup/solve phase. Judged memory-bandwidth bound / very-low arithmetic intensity (sparse stencil/SpMV kernels), poor cache reuse.

2. **amg2023 / cpu-mpi-openmp** — adds OpenMP threading inside each rank for local matrix assembly (evidenced by `hypre_NumActiveThreads`/`hypre_GetThreadNum` guarded blocks and CMake's `AMG_WITH_OMP`/`OpenMP::OpenMP_C`).

3. **amg2023 / mpi-cuda** — CUDA GPU build (`AMG_WITH_CUDA`, CUDA::cudart/cusolver/cublas/cusparse/curand, `HYPRE_DeviceInitialize`), one GPU per rank, Umpire device/UM memory pools.

4. **amg2023 / mpi-rocm** — HIP/ROCm GPU build (`AMG_WITH_HIP`, hip::device/host, roc::rocsparse/rocrand), targeting AMD GPUs on LLNL/ORNL systems per Makefile comments.

All traces note that the actual point-to-point halo-exchange/reduction implementation lives inside the externally-linked hypre library rather than in this repo, so communication-pattern specifics were inferred (medium confidence) from the decomposition parameters and observable barrier/timing calls rather than directly read point-to-point MPI code.
